 34NE c  Isotope discovery (2012Th10): Ta({+48}Ca,X) at RIKEN (2002No11) and    
 34NE2c  Ta({+48}Ca,X) at GANIL (2002Lu09).                                     
 34NE c  2002No11: Ta({+48}Ca,X) E=64 MeV/nucleon at RIKEN. Projectile fragments
 34NE2c  were separated and identified by the large-acceptance RIKEN            
 34NE3c  Projectile-Fragment Separator (RIPS). Measured production yield and    
 34NE4c  deduced production cross section of {+34}Ne to be |?0.1 pb. Also see   
 34NE5c  annual report 2002NoZY.                                                
 34NE c  2002Lu09: Ta({+48}Ca,X) E=59.8 MeV/nucleon at GANIL. Projectile        
 34NE2c  fragments were separated and identified by the LISE-2000 fragment      
 34NE3c  separator. Measured production yield and deduced production cross      
 34NE4c  section of {+34}Ne to be 0.17 pb {I12}. Also see 2002LuZT,2002Lu19,    
 34NE5c  2003Lu11, 2004Lu19.                                                    
 34NE c  2019Ah07: {+9}Be({+48}Ca,X) E=345 MeV/nucleon at RIKEN. Projectile     
 34NE2c  fragments were separated and identified using |DE-tof-B|r by the       
 34NE3c  large-acceptance two-stage separator BigRIPS. Optimum settings of B|r  
 34NE4c  were tuned to transmit {+33}F for 14 hours and {+36}Ne+{+39}Na for 7.8 
 34NE5c  hours. The Be target was irradiated with 1.4|*10{+17} and 7.8|*10{+16} 
 34NE6c  {+48}Ca ions, respectively. Measured Z vs A/Z particle-identification  
 34NE7c  plot. 115 {+34}Ne events were observed in the {+33}F setting, and 4    
 34NE8c  {+34}Ne events were observed in the {+36}Ne+{+39}Na setting. No {+35}Ne
 34NE9c  or {+36}Ne events were observed in either setting.                     
 34NE c  2022Ah02: Same experimental setup as 2019Ah07. Optimum settings of B|r 
 34NE2c  were tuned to transmit {+39}Na for 46.1 hours and {+36}Ne for 25.3     
 34NE3c  hours. Measured Z vs A/Z particle-identification plot. Some {+34}Ne    
 34NE4c  events were observed in the {+36}Ne setting. No {+35}Ne or {+36}Ne     
 34NE5c  events were observed in either setting. Also see review article        
 34NE6c  2025Ku15.                                                              
